# bsh playground

Press <CR> on a cell to run it. Re-run any cell to refresh its result in place:
the ```out / ```dir blocks below a cell belong to bsh. `za` folds a result.


## one-shot shell   (<CR> = inline output; g<CR> or <C-CR> = to a side buffer)

% echo "hello from a fresh shell"; uname -s

## try g<CR> here: output goes to a bsh://out buffer, <CR> on the ref opens it

% for i in $(seq 200); do echo "line $i"; done

## <C-c> cancels a running cell

% for i in 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9; do echo $i; sleep 1; done


## persistent session: env / cwd carry across %% cells (a plain % is fresh)

%% export GREETING=hi; cd /tmp
%% echo "$GREETING from $(pwd)"
% echo "a one-shot still runs in: $(pwd)"


## multiline (<CR> anywhere inside the fence)

```%%
for i in 1 2 3; do
  echo "line $i"
done
```


## python: one-shot (%) vs session (%%)

```python %
print("one-shot:", 2 ** 10)
```

```python %%
import math
r = 3
```

```python %%
print("area =", round(math.pi * r * r, 2))   # sees r + math from the cell above
```


## remote: put user@host (or an ssh alias) before the marker

<!-- me@myserver% uname -a -->
<!-- me@myserver: ~ -->


## files  (<CR> on an entry drills in / opens it; -T = foldable tree, -H = dotfiles)

: .

: .. -T


## your own commands: $BSH_HOME (point it at examples/bsh-home to try these)

demo.

demo.hello

demo.weather Ankara | tr a-z A-Z

demo.reverse hello

demo.menu

## foo.bar! opens a command's source (or scaffolds a new one, after a confirm)

demo.weather!


## agent (needs `pi`, or the `llm` CLI)

> say hello in one short sentence

>> now say it in French
